course: dictionary
lesson: 12770
title: Formal words about the church
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal. You meet them in old books, history lessons and on signs, and they sound grown-up. Do not panic. Look at the words around the hard word, because they are its context and they give clues. «The bishop wore ecclesiastical robes during the service.» Bishops, services and robes all belong to church life, so ecclesiastical must describe something that belongs to the church.
explain: Test your guess by swapping in a simple meaning. «The court dealt with ecclesiastical law» can become «the court dealt with church law», and it still makes sense, so your guess is right. A dictionary tells you the exact meaning: ecclesiastical means connected with the Christian church or its clergy, the priests, ministers and bishops.
explain: Ecclesiastical is an adjective, so it describes a noun. We can talk about ecclesiastical buildings, ecclesiastical law, ecclesiastical history and ecclesiastical architecture. In each phrase, the word tells you that the thing belongs to the church or its leaders.
fact: Ecclesiastical means connected with the Christian church or its clergy.
fact: The clergy are the priests, ministers and bishops who lead a church.
fact: «Ecclesiastical buildings» are churches, cathedrals and other buildings used by the church.
fact: «Ecclesiastical law» means the rules that the church sets for its own members and affairs.
fact: Ecclesiastical is a formal word, so you will see it more often in writing than in chatty talk.
exercise: «The bishop wore ecclesiastical robes during the service.» What does ecclesiastical mean here? | Very old and falling apart | Loud and cheerful | *Connected with the church | Made of silk and very shiny
exercise: «The ecclesiastical court met in the cathedral to settle a dispute about church land.» Where did the court meet? | *In the cathedral | At a railway station | In a school hall
exercise: Ella says, «We studied ecclesiastical architecture, like the tall stone church towers.» Which phrase is the best meaning? | Styles of clothes | Kinds of birds | *Building styles of churches | Ways to cook food
test: «The museum had a display of ecclesiastical history, with old prayer books and bells.» What does ecclesiastical history mean? | *Church history, as in the church's past | Story of a famous king | History of the church and its leaders | History of the sea and ships
test: Which word means connected with the church? | Secular | *Ecclesiastical | Municipal | Medieval
exam: Mia reads, «The ecclesiastical buildings in the town were built hundreds of years ago.» What does ecclesiastical describe, and what clue in the sentence helps you work it out? | It describes the shops, and the clue is town | It describes the trees, and the clue is ago | *It describes buildings connected with the church, and the clue is built | It describes the schools, and the clue is hundreds of years
